These are the files and lines this chapter followed, in reading order.

## One pixel, traced back {#c10 number=10 target=130 summary="The worked point P followed back through the frame in the engine's order, and three takeaways." sources="forward-targets, shadow-filter-default, forward-pixel, light-culling-pass, fullscreen-shadow, evaluate-lighting, diffuse-global, reflection-global, ssao-modulate, diffuse-specular-merge"}

### The frame, once more {#c10-map kind=2d graph=frame focus="DEPTH, CULL, SHADOW, FWD, TARGETS, DIFF, REFL, SSS, AO, MERGE, LUT, CUBES"}

Here is the frame again.

We follow one pixel through it, P, low on the teapot.

### P's light, in the order the engine made it {#c10-trace kind=3d}

${cue "key" {opening demoRoom panelHidden 0.6 {append baseLight {'
    {lightY 1.85}
    {lightZ 0.95}
    {lightX 0.55}
    {labels 0.0}
    {forwardStage 0.0}
    {extraLights 0.0}
    {cameraTarget {' -0.3 0.25 -1.6}}}}}}
${cue "key" {append teapotPoint {' {inspectObject 8.0} {pickShown 1.0}}}}
${cue "key" {'
    {motion {'
        {cameraPath {' {pose -22.0 18.0 2.8} {pose -34.0 14.0 3.0} {pose -18.0 20.0 2.6}}}}}}}

${cue "key" {' {inset "d"} {imageFar 3.0} {blend 2.0}}}
${cue "key" {chainTarget "d" 5.0 imageCornerTopLeft {'
    {imageFar 6.0}
    {imageTitle "views-depth_prepass"}}}}
${cue "key" {' {callout "depth-prepass"}}}
First the depth pre-pass wrote P's depth, and that depth chose P's depth bin inside its tile.

${cue "key" {' {glide sunYaw 55.0 sentence}}}
${cue "key" {'
    {inset "sb"}
    imageFromShadowBuffer
    {imageBlurred 1.0}
    imageCornerTopLeft
    {imageTitle "views-shadow_buffer"}}}
${cue "key" {' {callout "fullscreen-shadow"}}}
The shadow passes compared P against the sun's cascades and left one blurred number in the shadow buffer.

${cue "key" {' {glide extraLights 12.0 sentence}}}
${cue "key" {chainTarget "t0" 0.0 imageCornerBottomLeft {' {imageTitle "views-target_diffuse"}}}}
${cue "key" {' {callout "evaluate-lighting"}}}
The forward pass built P's surface, and walked the lights of its bin and the sun.

${cue "key" {' {inset "t0"} {imageTarget 2.0} {blend 1.5}}}
It wrote the resulting light, and the surface, into five targets.

${overCallout
    {' {forwardStageRange 0.0 1.0}}
    "diffuse-global"
    "The sky's diffuse light came from one lookup of the diffuse cubemap, along P's normal."}

${overCallout
    {' {forwardStageRange 1.0 2.0}}
    "reflection-global"
    "P's reflection came from the specular cubemap at the mip of P's roughness, scaled by the look-up texture's factor, F zero times A, plus B."}

${overCallout
    {' {forwardStageRange 2.0 3.0}}
    "ssao-modulate"
    "SSAO darkened P's diffuse light from fifty-two samples around it, twelve fixed and forty on the spiral."}

Then the merge pass of chapter one added diffuse and specular together.

### Three takeaways {#c10-takeaways kind=3d}

${cue "key" {opening demoRoom panelHidden 1.0 {append baseLight {'
    {sphereRoughness 0.35}
    {multiscatter 1.0}
    {ssaoRadius 0.05}
    {shadowBlur 1.0}
    {extraLights 0.0}
    {labels 0.0}
    {forwardStage 3.0}}}}}
${cue "key" {'
    {motion {'
        {cameraPath {' {pose 24.0 20.0 6.2} {pose 4.0 14.0 6.6} {pose -14.0 18.0 6.0}}}
        {path {' sunYaw} {' {' 70.0} {' 30.0}} beat}}}}}

${cue "key" {' {callout "forward-targets"}}}
The first takeaway is about the data the forward pass leaves.

${cue "key" {' {glide forwardStage 0.0 sentence}}}
The forward pass leaves a thin G-buffer of five targets and a stencil.

${cue "key" {' {glide forwardStage 3.0 sentence}}}
So full-screen passes can finish the light without drawing the scene again.

${cue "key" {' {callout "light-culling-pass"}}} The second is reuse.

${cue "key" {' {glide extraLights 24.0 sentence}}}
Lights are sorted once per tile, the sky and the BRDF are prefiltered once, and the sun's shadow is resolved once per pixel.

So each pixel pays only for what it reads.

${cue "key" {' {callout "shadow-filter-default"}}} The third is the trade-offs.

${cue "key" {' {shadowBlur 0.0} {blend 1.0}}}
The sun's shadow is a binary test, blurred in screen space.

${cue "key" {' {shadowBlur 1.0} {ssaoRadius 0.1} {blend 1.5}}}
The occlusion's radius is a share of the screen, not a distance, and the occlusion darkens direct light too.

${cue "key" {' {multiscatter 0.0} {sphereRoughness 0.9} {blend 1.5}}}
And the multiscatter compensation, which restores light lost between facets, is left off by default.

Each of these trades accuracy for speed.

${cue "key" {' {delay 0.5}}} That is how O3DE lights a frame.

### Where to read {#c10-sources kind=2d sources="forward-pixel, depth-prepass, light-culling-pass, fullscreen-shadow, evaluate-lighting, diffuse-global, reflection-global, ssao-modulate, diffuse-specular-merge"}

These are the functions the whole frame passes through, in the order a pixel meets them.
